---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="DroidDeck Guide — Troubleshooting & Compatibility Database"
  description="Independent DroidDeck troubleshooting & compatibility database. Device tests, error fixes, game compatibility lists, comparisons, and update notes for Android handhelds and Snapdragon phones."
  page="home"
>
  
  
    <section class="game-hero" id="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="hero-intro">
          <div>
            <div class="hero-label"><span></span> Independent Community Resource</div>
            <h1>DroidDeck Guide<span class="hero-subtitle">Troubleshooting &amp; Compatibility Database</span></h1>
            <p class="hero-slogan">Will it run?<br>How do I fix it?<br>What settings work best?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-explain">
            <h2>From the community, for the community</h2>
            <p>We test DroidDeck on real devices, collect error fixes, and maintain game compatibility lists so you spend less time troubleshooting and more time gaming.</p>
            <div class="actions">
              <a class="btn primary" href="/#devices"><i class="ri-smartphone-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Browse Devices</a>
              <a class="btn dark-outline" href="/#troubleshooting">Fix an Issue <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-notes">
              <span><i class="ri-check-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Device Test Reports</span>
              <span><i class="ri-check-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Error FAQ</span>
              <span><i class="ri-check-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Game Compatibility</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="hero-screen">
          <div class="screen-caption">
            <span><i class="ri-gamepad-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Real-device tests, clear answers</span>
            <span>COMPATIBILITY FIRST</span>
          </div>
          <img src="/assets/images/hero-screen.webp" alt="DroidDeck Steam Big Picture library" width="1440" height="667" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
        </figure>

        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <span>Independent guides for Android handhelds and Snapdragon phones</span>
          <a href="#local-gaming">Explore the database <i class="ri-arrow-down-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="capability-bar">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span><i class="ri-smartphone-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Device Tests</span>
        <span><i class="ri-bug-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Error Fixes</span>
        <span><i class="ri-gamepad-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Game Lists</span>
        <span><i class="ri-git-pull-request-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Version Notes</span>
        <span><i class="ri-scales-3-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Tool Comparisons</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="feature-story wrap" id="devices">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Device Compatibility</span>
          <h2>Know before you download</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Not every Android device runs DroidDeck well.<br>Our device pages answer the only question that matters: will it work on yours?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-grid">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <span class="section-number">01 / Device Test Reports</span>
          <h3>Real hardware,<br>real answers</h3>
          <p>Each device page includes hands-on results from the community: whether DroidDeck launches, which games are playable, recommended resolution and FSR settings, and known bugs.</p>
          <p>We focus on the devices people actually ask about — Android handhelds and Snapdragon flagship phones — and keep the data refreshed as new DroidDeck versions ship.</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Launch, stability, and thermal notes</li>
            <li>Recommended resolution and FSR presets</li>
            <li>Controller, keyboard, and touch mapping tips</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="/devices/ayn-odin-2/">See Ayn Odin 2 report <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="story-visual">
          <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge device compatibility screenshot">
            <img src="/assets/images/game-management.webp" alt="DroidDeck game management screen" width="1280" height="614" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
          </button>
          <figcaption>DroidDeck game management</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="device-grid">
        <article>
          <i class="ri-smartphone-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3>Ayn Odin 2</h3>
          <p>Snapdragon 8 Gen 2 handheld. Solid DroidDeck performer with good thermals.</p>
          <a href="/devices/ayn-odin-2/">Read report</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <i class="ri-smartphone-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3>Retroid Pocket 5</h3>
          <p>Snapdragon 865-based device. Check GPU compatibility before heavy titles.</p>
          <a href="/devices/retroid-pocket-5/">Read report</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <i class="ri-smartphone-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3>Ayaneo Pocket S</h3>
          <p>Snapdragon G3x Gen 2. Premium build, great for demanding games.</p>
          <a href="/devices/ayaneo-pocket-s/">Read report</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <i class="ri-cpu-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3>Snapdragon 8 Gen 3 Phones</h3>
          <p>Latest flagships with Adreno 750. Best raw performance for phones.</p>
          <a href="/devices/snapdragon-8-gen-3/">Read report</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="control-story" id="troubleshooting">
      <div class="wrap control-grid">
        <figure>
          <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge troubleshooting interface screenshot">
            <img src="/assets/images/controller-mapping.webp" alt="DroidDeck touch controller editor" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
          </button>
          <figcaption>Touch controller mapping</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="control-copy">
          <span class="section-number">02 / Error Fixes</span>
          <h2>Stuck? Start here.</h2>
          <p>Black screen, crash on launch, Steam login failures, missing storage, unrecognized controllers, audio stutter — we break each problem into symptoms, causes, and step-by-step fixes.</p>
          <div class="control-options">
            <span><i class="ri-bug-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Black screen</span>
            <span><i class="ri-bug-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Crashes</span>
            <span><i class="ri-bug-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Steam login</span>
            <span><i class="ri-bug-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> No sound</span>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/troubleshooting/black-screen/">Fix black screen <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="gallery-area wrap" id="games">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Explore the Database</span>
          <h2>Five ways to find answers</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Browse by device, error, game, comparison, or update.<br>Each section is built for search and for quick reference.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery-layout">
        <div class="gallery-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Database sections">
          <button role="tab" id="tab-devices" aria-controls="panel-devices" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">
            <span>01</span>
            <div><strong>Devices</strong><small>Test reports &amp; settings</small></div>
            <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-troubleshooting" aria-controls="panel-troubleshooting" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">
            <span>02</span>
            <div><strong>Troubleshooting</strong><small>Error fixes &amp; FAQ</small></div>
            <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-games" aria-controls="panel-games" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">
            <span>03</span>
            <div><strong>Games</strong><small>Compatibility lists</small></div>
            <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-compare" aria-controls="panel-compare" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">
            <span>04</span>
            <div><strong>Compare</strong><small>DroidDeck vs others</small></div>
            <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-updates" aria-controls="panel-updates" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">
            <span>05</span>
            <div><strong>Updates</strong><small>Release notes &amp; bugs</small></div>
            <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-panels">
          <figure role="tabpanel" id="panel-devices" aria-labelledby="tab-devices">
            <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge devices panel">
              <img src="/assets/images/steam-library.webp" alt="Steam Big Picture library" width="1440" height="667" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
            </button>
            <figcaption>Device pages list real test results and recommended settings.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure role="tabpanel" id="panel-troubleshooting" aria-labelledby="tab-troubleshooting" hidden>
            <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge troubleshooting panel">
              <img src="/assets/images/game-management.webp" alt="DroidDeck game management" width="1280" height="614" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
            </button>
            <figcaption>Each error gets its own page with symptoms, causes, and fixes.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure role="tabpanel" id="panel-games" aria-labelledby="tab-games" hidden>
            <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge games panel">
              <img src="/assets/images/hero-screen.webp" alt="DroidDeck Steam library" width="1440" height="667" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
            </button>
            <figcaption>Game lists separate indie 60 FPS titles from demanding AAA games.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure role="tabpanel" id="panel-compare" aria-labelledby="tab-compare" hidden>
            <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge compare panel">
              <img src="/assets/images/controller-mapping.webp" alt="DroidDeck controller mapping" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
            </button>
            <figcaption>Compare DroidDeck with Winlator and Mobox to choose the right tool.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure role="tabpanel" id="panel-updates" aria-labelledby="tab-updates" hidden>
            <button class="zoom-button" aria-label="Enlarge updates panel">
              <img src="/assets/images/game-management-detail.webp" alt="DroidDeck game management detail" width="1280" height="614" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <span class="zoom-hint"><i class="ri-fullscreen-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> View larger</span>
            </button>
            <figcaption>Every release gets translated notes plus a community bug roundup.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="getting-started" id="compare">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <span class="kicker">Choosing a Tool</span>
            <h2>DroidDeck vs the alternatives</h2>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/compare/">Read full comparison <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>DroidDeck</h3>
            <p class="tag">Steam-first · ARM64 native</p>
            <p>Best if you want a SteamOS-like experience on Android, native ARM64 Steam client, and integrated controller mapping.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Winlator</h3>
            <p class="tag">Box-based · Broad compatibility</p>
            <p>Strong for running non-Steam Windows apps and games. Heavier setup, more manual tuning.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>MoboX</h3>
            <p class="tag">Termux-based · PC environment</p>
            <p>Good for users comfortable with Linux/Termux workflows. Larger environment overhead.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-area wrap" id="faq">
      <div class="faq-intro">
        <span class="kicker">Common Questions</span>
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <p>Quick answers about the site,<br>compatibility, and how to contribute.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/troubleshooting/">Browse all fixes <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Is this the official DroidDeck website? <i class="ri-add-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>No. DroidDeck Guide is an independent community resource. The official site is <a href="https://droiddeck.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">droiddeck.app</a>. We focus on troubleshooting and compatibility data, not the download itself.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What devices can run DroidDeck? <i class="ri-add-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>DroidDeck runs on Android 9+ devices with Adreno 730 or newer GPUs. Snapdragon 8 Gen 2/Gen 3 phones and Android handhelds like Ayn Odin 2, Retroid Pocket 5, and Ayaneo Pocket S are popular choices. Mali and Google Tensor GPUs are not officially supported.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need a PC or root access? <i class="ri-add-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>No PC streaming and no root required. DroidDeck runs games locally on your Android device. Some devices need a one-time sub-process limit adjustment on first setup.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is the compatibility data collected? <i class="ri-add-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>We combine community reports, Reddit/Discord discussions, and our own tests. Each page marks entries as "Verified" or "Community Report" so you know how confident we are.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I contribute a test result? <i class="ri-add-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>Yes. Use the feedback link in the footer or reach out on Discord. Include your device, DroidDeck version, game, settings, and the result.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How often is the database updated? <i class="ri-add-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>We aim to publish translated release notes and a bug roundup within 48 hours of each new DroidDeck release. Device and game pages are reviewed quarterly or when a major bug is reported.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="download-area" id="updates">
      <div class="wrap download-inner">
        <div>
          <span class="download-kicker">Stay in the loop</span>
          <h2>Get the latest compatibility notes.</h2>
          <p>New DroidDeck releases can change what works. We translate changelogs and round up new bugs so you know before you update.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn primary" href="/updates/"><i class="ri-git-pull-request-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Latest Updates</a>
            <a class="btn dark-outline" href="https://droiddeck.app/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Official Download <i class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="download-qr">
          <div class="qr-placeholder"><i class="ri-qr-code-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <figcaption>Scan for official download</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
  
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "name": "DroidDeck Guide",
        "url": "https://droiddeck-guide.gg/",
        "description": "Independent DroidDeck troubleshooting & compatibility database."
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {"@type":"Question","name":"What devices can run DroidDeck?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"DroidDeck runs on Android 9+ devices with Adreno 730 or newer GPUs. Snapdragon 8 Gen 2/Gen 3 phones and Android handhelds like Ayn Odin 2, Retroid Pocket 5, and Ayaneo Pocket S are popular choices."}},
          {"@type":"Question","name":"Does DroidDeck need a PC or root?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. DroidDeck runs games locally on your Android device without streaming from a PC. Root is not required, though some devices need a one-time sub-process setup."}},
          {"@type":"Question","name":"Is this the official DroidDeck website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. DroidDeck Guide is an independent community resource focused on troubleshooting and compatibility. The official site is droiddeck.app."}}
        ]
      }
    ]
  })} />
</Layout>
